---
import SiteLayout from "@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Security — Najd Research"
  description="Security reporting and product security commitments for Najd Research."
>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="page-shell header-inner">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Najd Research home"
        ><img
          class="wordmark-logo"
          src="/logo.webp"
          alt=""
          width="96"
          height="49"
        /><span>Najd Research</span></a
      ><nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="/code">Najd Code <span>01</span></a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main id="main-content" class="document-shell page-shell">
    <header class="document-hero">
      <p class="kicker">POLICY / SECURITY</p><h1>
        Report security issues privately.
      </h1><p class="document-lede">
        Please do not disclose a suspected vulnerability publicly before we have
        had time to investigate and coordinate a fix.
      </p>
    </header>
    <article class="policy-copy">
      <h2>Reporting</h2><p>
        Send a clear description, affected version, reproduction steps, and
        impact to <a href="mailto:security@najdresearch.com"
          >security@najdresearch.com</a
        >. Do not include credentials or unrelated personal data.
      </p>
      <h2>Release boundary</h2><p>
        Najd Code releases require pinned source revisions, checksum-verified
        runtimes, dependency and license evidence, native UI acceptance, signed
        artifacts, notarization, and a release soak against the exact published
        bytes.
      </p>
      <h2>Product boundary</h2><p>
        Local services bind to loopback interfaces and authenticate requests.
        Remote execution uses registered repositories and mutually authenticated
        nodes. Enterprise policy and audit features are separately licensed and
        self-hosted.
      </p>
      <h2>Safe harbor</h2><p>
        Good-faith research that avoids privacy violations, service disruption,
        and access beyond what is necessary to demonstrate the issue will not be
        pursued by Najd Research.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <footer>
    <div class="page-shell document-footer">
      <p>Najd Research · Riyadh, Saudi Arabia</p><div>
        <a href="/code">Najd Code</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</SiteLayout>
